# t0942 — the `unit` / `*mut unit` REPRESENTATIONS of a Callable. `.clone()` on
# these SEGVs and NO `GirType::FnPtr` arm can reach them, so t0936's fix (which
# heals the FnPtr cells) leaves these RED by construction.
#
#   Callable[int(int)] cb       PARAMETER        -> GIR `unit`
#   Callable[int(int)] &cb      PARAMETER        -> GIR `*mut unit`
#   int(int) f = dbl            bare fn-type     -> GIR `unit`
#
# src/ir/lowering/types.rs:190-205 states all three and gives the verification
# command (`gg build --emit-gir`).
#
# ⛔ DO NOT "FIX" THIS WITH A `GirType::Unit` ARM in the dispatch-name ladder:
# that routes EVERY unit-typed receiver through the closure clone path and is a
# strictly worse miscompile than the bug. The representation must carry the
# type, which is an upstream (erasure) fix.
#
# ggdef adjudicates the param cell correctly (prints 2).
# INTENDED: prints 2.
int apply_it(Callable[int(int)] cb):
    Callable[int(int)] g = cb.clone()
    return g(1)

void main():
    print(apply_it((int x): x + 1))
